# STRESS 05b — NESTING, GAP AND THE BOX MODEL
#
# The other half of sizing: what happens when boxes contain boxes, what `gap`
# takes out of an axis, and where padding, border and margin go.
#
# DESIGN.md D4: sizing is ALWAYS border-box. `height: 60pt` means the border
# box is 60pt, so padding and border eat into the content and never inflate the
# box. Margin is the only one that claims extra room, and margins never
# collapse.

page
  size: letter
  margin: 0.45in

defaults
  font: IBM Plex Mono
  font-size: 7pt
  color: gray(0.12)

style bar
  height: 26pt
  border-width: 0.4pt
  border-color: gray(0.55)
  valign: middle
  align: center

section
  height: 28pt
  text "05b · NESTING, GAP AND THE BOX MODEL"
    font-size: 14pt
    font-weight: bold
    tracking: 1.2pt

section
  height: 40pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Five levels of nesting, each 80% of its parent and inset 6pt. The innermost box is 0.8^5 = 32.8% of the outer width, and every edge is still on a whole tick."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 130pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: fill
      border-width: 0.5pt
      border-color: gray(0.3)
      padding: 6pt
      column
        width: 80%
        box
          height: fill
          border-width: 0.5pt
          border-color: gray(0.4)
          padding: 6pt
          column
            width: 80%
            box
              height: fill
              border-width: 0.5pt
              border-color: gray(0.5)
              padding: 6pt
              column
                width: 80%
                box
                  height: fill
                  border-width: 0.5pt
                  border-color: gray(0.6)
                  padding: 6pt
                  column
                    width: 80%
                    box
                      height: fill
                      border-width: 0.5pt
                      border-color: gray(0.7)
                      line-style: ruled
                      line-pitch: 5mm
                      line-color: gray(0.85)
                  column
                    width: 20%
              column
                width: 20%
          column
            width: 20%
      column
        width: 20%

section
  height: 32pt
  valign: bottom
  text "gap comes off the top of the axis before anything else is resolved: it is structural, not negotiable. Four fill columns at three gaps."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 30pt
  gap: 0pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
      text "gap: 0"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar

section
  height: 32pt
  padding-top: 4pt
  gap: 6pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
      text "gap: 6pt"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar

section
  height: 32pt
  padding-top: 4pt
  gap: 18pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
      text "gap: 18pt"
        align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar
  column
    width: fill
    box
      style: bar

section
  height: 32pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Border-box sizing (D4): every box below is declared 60pt tall. Padding and border eat into the content; they never inflate the box. Margin is the one that does take extra room, and margins never collapse."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 84pt
  gap: 10pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 60pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      line-style: ruled
      line-pitch: 5mm
      line-color: gray(0.85)
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 60pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      padding: 10pt
      line-style: ruled
      line-pitch: 5mm
      line-color: gray(0.85)
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 60pt
      border-width: 3pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      line-style: ruled
      line-pitch: 5mm
      line-color: gray(0.85)
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 60pt
      margin: 8pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      line-style: ruled
      line-pitch: 5mm
      line-color: gray(0.85)

section
  height: 14pt
  gap: 10pt
  column
    width: fill
    text "plain"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
  column
    width: fill
    text "padding: 10pt"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
  column
    width: fill
    text "border-width: 3pt"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
  column
    width: fill
    text "margin: 8pt"
      font-size: 6pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center

section
  height: 32pt
  valign: bottom
  text "Padding takes CSS shorthand arity — one, two or four values — and a per-side property refines one edge of whatever the shorthand said. The inner box shows where the content actually starts."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 78pt
  gap: 10pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 62pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      padding: 10pt
      box
        height: fill
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        line-style: ruled
        line-pitch: 4mm
        line-color: gray(0.85)
    text "padding: 10pt"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 62pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      padding: 4pt 16pt
      box
        height: fill
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        line-style: ruled
        line-pitch: 4mm
        line-color: gray(0.85)
    text "padding: 4pt 16pt"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 62pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      padding: 2pt 8pt 16pt 24pt
      box
        height: fill
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        line-style: ruled
        line-pitch: 4mm
        line-color: gray(0.85)
    text "2pt 8pt 16pt 24pt"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
      padding-top: 3pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 62pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      padding: 8pt
      padding-left: 28pt
      box
        height: fill
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        line-style: ruled
        line-pitch: 4mm
        line-color: gray(0.85)
    text "8pt, then padding-left 28pt"
      font-size: 5.5pt
      color: gray(0.4)
      align: center
      padding-top: 3pt

section
  height: 32pt
  valign: bottom
  text "valign on a container decides where the leftover height goes when nothing on the axis was flexible. `spacer fill` is the other way to say it, and it is the one that works when only part of the stack should move."
    font-size: 7.5pt
    color: gray(0.45)

section
  height: 96pt
  gap: 10pt
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: top
      box
        height: 18pt
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        align: center
        valign: middle
        text "valign: top"
          font-size: 6pt
          align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: middle
      box
        height: 18pt
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        align: center
        valign: middle
        text "valign: middle"
          font-size: 6pt
          align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      valign: bottom
      box
        height: 18pt
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        align: center
        valign: middle
        text "valign: bottom"
          font-size: 6pt
          align: center
  column
    width: fill
    box
      height: 82pt
      border-width: 0.4pt
      border-color: gray(0.55)
      box
        height: 18pt
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        align: center
        valign: middle
        text "top"
          font-size: 6pt
          align: center
      spacer
        height: fill
      box
        height: 18pt
        border-width: 0.4pt
        border-color: gray(0.3)
        align: center
        valign: middle
        text "spacer fill, then this"
          font-size: 6pt
          align: center

section
  height: fill
  valign: bottom
  text "Every edge on this sheet is a whole number of ticks. Five nested 80% splits of a 522pt content width give 171.06pt at the innermost level, which is 2737 ticks — and the sum of each level's two children is still exactly its parent, because DistributeTicks apportions rather than multiplies."
    font-size: 6.5pt
    color: gray(0.5)
